### EarlyAttestationBleed and EarlyAttestationTschüss
- **Presenter:** Muhammad Usama Sardar (joint work with Songbo)
- **Slides:** [EarlyAttestationBleed and EarlyAttestationTschüss](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ufmrg-earlyattestationbleed-and-earlyattestationtschuss-00)
- **Discussion:**
  - Muhammad Usama Sardar presented a formal symbolic security analysis using ProVerif on early attestation protocols in confidential computing frameworks (e.g., Contrast, MarbleRun, Constellation) and draft specifications based on RFC 9261 (Exported Authenticators for TLS).
  - Under an endpoint adversary model (where the host operating system outside the TEE is untrusted), early attestation designs binding attestation to Handshake Traffic Secrets fail to guarantee application security.
  - Formal analysis demonstrated that attestation must be cryptographically bound to the Application Traffic Secret (ATSC).
  - Found critical-severity vulnerabilities (CVSS 9.1–9.6) leading to multiple CVEs and security advisories.
  - Impact on implementations and standards:
    - Multiple open-source implementations (RustLS, Go libraries, Cocos AI, Confidential Computing Consortium attestation SIG) have retired or archived early attestation in favor of post-handshake attestation.
    - The SATI TLS attestation draft was withdrawn, and related early attestation EAT profiles were updated or archived.

